    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0464" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg150"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Cairo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-12">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>When the Khedive assumes authority, you will deal with him
                    as a <hi rendition="#italic">de-facto</hi> official, but do not attend the
                    ceremonies. You can show <pb facs="0465" n="151" xml:id="pg151"/> this telegram
                    unofficially to the British authorities and explain that this action is taken
                    out of scrupulous regard for neutrality.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
